\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  He is blessed that conquer sin,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And Christ's messenger too,
\par He suffered under transgression
\par But Christ has redeemed him.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Much gloom belies the gloom of sin,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 The way is closed entirely,
\par The upright road in Jesus Christ,
\par Takes one right through His blood.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  The worship of sin doth covet,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Hatred and strife abound,
\par They serve and struggle after such,
\par Jesus console them all.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  The benefits of sinful acts,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Is naught but painful death,
\par  Our mediator is Jesus Christ,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 In Him is life as well.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O, Redeemer, I shall love Thee,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I owe Thee salvation,
\par I know not whom to serve again,
\par I was baptized in Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The Redeemed has liberty,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And forgiveness of sins,
\par I shall therefore praise Thee daily,
\par Thy glory is supreme!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. I'll serve Thee Jesus Christ alone,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I am Thine own, I say,
\par I shall abide with Thee daily,
\par \pard     And draw pleasure fromThee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

